# Binsec/Rel constant-time check for x25519_field_sq (Tier B per ADR-0009).
#
# x25519_field_sq is currently a wrapper for x25519_field_mul(a, a): it copies
# the input pointer from a1 to a2, then tail-calls the full multiplication and
# reduction routine. Field-element limbs are secret during the X25519 ladder.
# This proof starts at the wrapper entry and halts at the tail-called field_mul
# return, checking the wrapper plus the compiled RV32IMC multiplication body for
# secret-independent control flow and memory-access addresses.

starting from <x25519_field_sq> with
  sp := 0x90000000
  ra := 0xDEADBEEF
  a0 := 0x80000000          # out (40 bytes)
  a1 := 0x80001000          # a   (40 bytes)
  for i<32> in 0 to 9 do
    @[a1 + i * 4, 4] := secret as a_limb
  end
end

# field_sq tail-calls field_mul, so the return instruction lives in the callee.
halt at <x25519_field_mul> return

explore all
